# Create PR

When creating or updating a GitHub pull request, follow `.cursor/skills/create-pr/SKILL.md`. Create a ticket **only** when the task is entirely new **and** no GitHub issue (open or closed) already covers it. If one exists, link `Closes #N` / `Related to #N`. Never duplicate. Never write “Hors backlog”.

The description is always in French, with this section order: Ticket, Résumé, Preview Storybook, Tests, Accessibilité, Breaking changes. Do not use English headings such as Summary or Test plan. Title stays an English conventional commit. Ticket must be `Closes #N` (never “Hors backlog”). After create or edit, run `.github/scripts/sync-project-status.sh <pr-number>` (`project-status`).
